<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stefan Dragutin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1244–<a href="/years/1316">1316</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stefan Dragutin was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> from 1276 to 1282, when a riding accident led him to hand power to his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-milutin">Stefan Milutin</a>. Married to a Hungarian princess, he received the Banate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macva">Mačva</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a> from the Hungarian crown in 1284 and ruled the northern lands as a separate realm, sometimes called the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syrmia">Syrmia</a>, until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stefan-dragutin.jpg" alt="Stefan Dragutin" width="279" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fresco_of_Stefan_Dragutin,_Arilje.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
